{"reference":"1 Chronicles 28","book":"1 Chronicles","chapter":28,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"David and the Temple","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"David tells Israel that he was not permitted to build the temple because he was a man of war who had shed blood. Chronicles gives this explanation in a form not given in Nathan’s oracle in 2 Samuel 7, so both presentations should be retained rather than treating one as a replacement for the other. The chapter also emphasizes that David still prepared extensively for Solomon’s work, providing plans, materials, personnel, and public support for the temple project.","verse_refs":["1 Chronicles 28:1-21","1 Chronicles 28:2-7"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_chronicles_028_c5d483199d6887c5a0759b86"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}